Due to his poor Extraction stats, Blot is best utilized as a Distractor due to his high mobility, having 4 Movement Speed and 5 Star Stamina. However, he can also be proficient in the Support and Survivalist category due to his unique Active Ability, **Blot Jr.**, which can potentially even save you or your teammates from death if used correctly. In general, Blot can be a pretty good Distractor/Support/Survivalist, with his only main downsides being his 1 Star Skill Check and 2 Star Extraction Speed.

Blot's main specialty is his Ability. **Blot Jr.** is a decoy that diverts Twisteds attention on activation; This also takes aggro off of other Toons, even Shrimpo, as **Blot Jr.** has an astoundingly low -999 Stealth. This can basically be used as a "stun" tool, since when Blot Jr. is killed by a Twisted, that Twisted's attack waiting time will apply as if it attacked a regular Toon, giving you time to run away. Do note that if a Main Character or Lethal Twisted kills **Blot Jr.**, their attack sound plays, so be sure to tell your teammates that it was your decoy, and not an actual Toon, as this can temporarily cause panic. It should also be noted that, if you have multiple Twisteds chasing you and activate **Blot Jr.**, they will all start going toward the decoy, but their attention will immediately divert back to you; only the Twisted who attacked Blot Jr. will be "stunned." It's recommended to get a decently large distance away, then activate **Blot Jr.** and go around a corner of an island nearby. If Blot Jr. is undisturbed, he will automatically die after 10 seconds; if you plan on placing him at a location ahead of time, make sure to time it so he can actually grab aggro when a teammate passes by a certain area (for example, near the Elevator to help a distractor or teammates in a chase more safely enter).

It's important to remember that Blot Jr. won't save you or others from long-ranged Twisted attacks ( Twisted Goob, Twisted Gigi, and Twisted Scraps), Twisted Squirm's grab, activated Twisted Razzle & Dazzle, activated Twisted Rodger, Twisted Blot's hands, or placed traps ( Twisted Sprout and Twisted Bassie). However, Blot Jr. can put the 3 long-ranged Twisted's attacks on cooldown if they hit him, which could be useful if they threaten to corner anyone, or are near the Elevator. He can also use Blot Jr. to force Twisted Sprout into spawning a tendril, controlling the location to prevent it from being somewhere inconvenient or dangerous (such as under a Machine).

It is advised not to use **Blot Jr.** near where your distractor is distracting unless you are given express permission (like Panic Mode), as it can pull the Twisteds away from them, which could potentially endanger the team.

**Blot Jr.** can be used in a specific few ways, such as:

•"Stunning" a Twisted chasing you or someone else, giving you/them time to escape;

•At Panic Mode, to divert a Twisted's attention away from Toons trying to get in the Elevator;

•As a less effective Air Horn, as you can place Blot Jr. behind a Toon being chased to "stun" the Twisted, and then take aggro. Note this is less effective than using an actual Air Horn, especially with multiple Twisteds;

•Taking aggro of Twisteds away from a Toon, and then using **Blot Jr.** to run away. Don't do this for a Distractor though, as this can mess up their loop;

•Rounding up the Twisteds, placing your decoy and giving them to your distractor so they don't waste Stamina gathering them;

•If you're attempting the TIME'S UP challenge card, your decoy can reset Twisted Dyle's speed, and/or buy time for you or your teammates to escape.

**Blot Jr.** costs 10-80 Tapes depending on how many alive Blots there are in a round, so it's not a good idea to have a significant amount of them in a run. This can also cause resource strain if Sprout is present, as the already large amount of Tapes he needs, combined with the fact each Blot in-game will need a larger amount of tapes for decoys, is likely to result in Tapes having to be spread out evenly, meaning both Sprout and each Blot in-game will get fewer Tapes. However, if there's only 1-3 Blots present (cost being at 30 if 3 are present), then this shouldn't be too much of an issue, since **Blot Jr.** will be decently cheap and be usable almost immediately.

Blot can be a good distractor in Ichor Leaks due to his immunity to the Slow I and Ichor Stains, negating the risk of lost speed, as well as obscured vision. This is all without the need for Train Whistle (though it can still help when distracting Twisted Vee). Therefore you could volunteer to distract in Ichor Leaks, if you’re a backup distractor, giving the main distractor a break or letting them handle slower Twisteds.

Blot has more advantages compared to other Toons in Dyle runs. His high Movement Speed and Stamina stats provide great survivability, and as said above he can reset Twisted Dyle's speed meter in sticky situations and buy time. While his subpar extraction stats can hinder him, especially his 1 Star Skill Check, this can be easily negated with Mime Makeup, eased with Thinking Cap, and ignorable altogether with Treadmill Machines.

Overall, Blot is a good pick for Distracting and Surviving (due to his Stats being very similar to other survivalists and distractors), as well as Supporting.

