• **Scrapbook**, to be able to distract without other 2 Stealth Toons taking aggro off you;

•Only use this Trinket combo if most of the players in your run have 2 Star Stealth, or if you're solar distracting with a Bobette lacking Diary.

•Any of the Trinkets in the **Extraction Section**, to help with Floor progression; etc.

**Extraction**

• **Magnifying Glass/Options**

•This Trinket allows Goob to take full advantage over his 2 Extraction Speed (0.85 extraction speed) and 3 Star Skill Check (100.5 skill check size). Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:

• **Vee's Remote**, to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote;

• **Participation Award**, to speed up Machine completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction (27.95 avg/24.84 with Tech Savvy);

•Any Trinkets listed in the **Distraction** section, to help with survival.

**Ability/Support**

• **Ghost Snakes In A Can**, to reduce **Hug!**'s Ability cooldown (25s).

• **Sweet Charm**, to further reduce **Hug!**'s cooldown, though only by a small amount as the Trinket works with percentages (22.6s).

Scraps possesses the best Stamina stat in the game (tied with Sprout, Bobette, and Blot) and an Ability that has the potential to help her escape from Twisteds or to quickly get to the Elevator during Panic Mode or get to Machines faster—granted there's another Toon or Machine nearby. These traits make her best suited to Survival. While her below-average Movement Speed does partially negate her large Stamina pool, Items like Speed Candies or Boxes o' Chocolates and Trinkets such as Pink Bow are more than capable of turning her into a force to be reckoned with. Otherwise, she doesn't excel at anything in particular.

Hovering your mouse over nearby Toons on PC or being in their proximity on Mobile can quickly identify players or Machines with a white outline to grapple onto them. This is useful for noticing teammates through walls, but remember that her **Crafty Grapple** Ability requires line of sight, however, if the target moves behind an object, you will continue to move to their location when you had initially grappled anyways. This could also work on Machines, but it is less efficient as you cannot rely on Machines to spawn in the right spots every run and grappling on Machines should more often than not be used if planning to extract them, but it is still a helpful tool. On later Floors, where Machine count increases, escape becomes easier due to the abundance of things to grapple onto. However, do keep in mind that in Blackouts, there may be Twisteds near the Machine that may hit you right after using your Ability due to its slight endlag. It also takes about ~0.8 seconds for you to move towards the Machine after activating the Ability, so a bit of distance if you are being chased is welcome.

While she does have 5 Stamina, her 2 Star Movement Speed can conflict a lot, making her only outrun the Twisteds by a little bit as well as making it hard to lose sight of them. It is heavily recommended to use Run Speed Trinkets such as Pink Bow (24.2 run speed), Speedy Shoes (23.125 run speed). With this, she can have lots of Stamina to run as well as having enough Run Speed to get away. Using Clown Horn/ Ribbon Spool together is also good, but it will take both of your Trinket slots, though it comes at the benefit of 24.75 Run Speed, almost 3 Star Run Speed. Though, if you still want a Trinket slot open for something else, Pink Bow would probably be the best option out of these in terms of consistency. Ghost Snakes In A Can can also be a good choice, especially in later Floors where more Machines spawn, allowing for even quicker travel across Floors, and taking advantage of the invincibility frames more often through her Ability, though it doesn't directly boost her Movement Speed, only general traversal.

One niche Scraps is very good at is passing Twisteds to distractors, primarily coming down to her average Stealth and Ability. Since the most common distractor choices have 2 or 3 Stars in Stealth, she can easily pass Twisteds to them. When passing to 3 Star Toons, she can bring the Twisted towards their distraction area or near the distractor directly, before grappling to a faraway Machine or player, thus swapping the distance priority. Due to her invincibility frames while grappling, this can also allow her to pass faster Twisteds and ranged Twisteds more safely. When passing to 2 Star Stealth Toons, she could instead opt to grapple directly to the distractor. If she has Diary equipped, she can use this exact strategy for 3 Star Stealth distractors as well. When combined with a Movement Speed increase from an Item or Trinket (such as Pink Bow), and her 5 Star Stamina, she can pass practically any Twisted to a distractor. This may not be applicable with a distractor who has 4+ Stars in Stealth, but she could possibly bring the Twisteds to the distractor, followed by U-turning around a corner or island by grappling. Although Glisten and Flutter could theoretically outdo her with this, thanks to their higher speeds, and Glisten's teleportation through walls, both of them don't get invincibility frames with their Abilities, have longer cooldowns, and Glisten has lower Stealth.

Since Scraps' Ability gives her invincibility frames while she's grappling, it does allow her to make certain moves that many other Toons can't. She can bait or pass by long-ranged Twisteds ( Twisted Goob and Twisted Scraps) without having to hide behind cover, since she could just grapple to a Machine/player. She can quickly leave the ranges of Twisted Rodger and Twisted Razzle & Dazzle, though the 2 Star Movement Speed could still be an issue. She can also pass straight through Twisted Blot's hands and Twisted Sprout's tendrils. Keep in mind that these do require a Machine or other Toon that is close enough to be in range.

Scraps isn't the best Toon for completing Dyle's Floor; her lower mobility and Skill Check both pose large disadvantages, as she will struggle to get away from Twisteds (though this is somewhat mitigated by her Stamina stat) and her 2 Star Skill Check could put you at risk if you aren't good at hitting them, not to mention the +50 Stamina the Floor gives is really unnecessary for her. Though, she does have a niche at the same time, as the abundant amount of Machines scattered around the Floor can allow for quick traversal and escapes, thanks to her Ability's cooldown. If you struggle with survivability in terms of Movement Speed, Glisten may be a better alternative, as he has 3 Star Movement Speed and can extract much faster. His Ability's much longer cooldown, as well it not working on Machines, the 2 Star Stealth stat and shared Skill Check stat could make the switch kind of iffy.

If you want to enhance Scraps' Extraction, using Vee's Remote is a great option as the Floor can progress faster. Her below-average extractability makes extracting quite difficult for her, so, if other extractors are present, ask them to do your Machine, and use the time saved to find other Machines or run to the Elevator before Panic Mode begins.

Note that Scraps' stat spread is quite medicore. 2 Star Skill Check coupled with 3 Star Extraction makes the extraction process a bit slow, and 2 Star Movement Speed makes her high Stamina less beneficial (being able to run for longer won't help if you can't outrun a fast Twisted like Twisted Pebble). While these weaknesses can be mitigated with Trinkets and awareness, Scraps is generally overshadowed by most Toons who can extract faster and possess even better survival. Scraps' main advantage over others is her Stamina, but Stamina isn't a good stat to invest Stars in due to both Well-Paced and Endurance cards giving 20 Stamina and TIMES UP with 50, adding up to almost 3 extra Stars in Stamina. Additionally, though Scraps can traverse faster via Crafty Grapple, one may be better off with higher movement speed instead.

**Trinket Combinations**

For specific Trinket recommendations, here are some possible combinations:

**Survivability**

• **Pink Bow/Options**

•This Trinket enables Scraps to outrun all Twisteds but Twisted Bobette, Twisted Gourdy, and Twisted Dyle before Panic Mode (24.2 run speed). Here are some options to pair Pink Bow with:

• **Speedy Shoes**, to outrun Twisted Bobette before Panic Mode (25.3 run speed);

• **Vanity Mirror**, to outrun every Twisted except Twisted Bobette during Panic Mode except for Twisted Gourdy (without Suppression) and Twisted Dyle (31.4 run speed);

• **Diary**, to not interfere with 3 Stealth Distractors;

•Only use this Trinket set if there is a distractor that meets such criteria in the first place.

• **Train Whistle**, to make escaping with the Slow Debuff easier without losing much Stamina;

• **Star Pillow**, to regenerate Stamina faster while extracting, taking advantage of her high Stamina and slow extraction;

•Any of the Trinkets in the **Extraction Section**, to help with Floor progression; etc.

**Extraction**

• **Magnifying Glass/Options**

•This Trinket allows Scraps to take full advantage over her 3 Extraction Speed (1.00 Extraction Speed) and 2 Star Skill Check (67 Skill Check size). Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:

• **Vee's Remote**, to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote;

• **Participation Award**, to speed up Machine completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction. However, it leaves you with a near 1 Star Window Size (27.11 avg/24.1 with Tech Savvy);

• **Thinking Cap**, to increase Skill Check size, helping you hit your Skill Checks easier if you struggle with such;

• **Mime Makeup**, to avoid attracting Twisteds to your location when you miss a Skill Check, also helps if you desire to complete Dyle's Floor at ease;

•Any Trinkets listed in the **Survivability/Mobility** section, to help with survival.

**Ability**

• **Ghost Snakes In A Can/ Peppermint Icing**

•The cooldown reduction synergizes with Peppermint Icing, allowing Scraps to regain Stamina more often. With the Rehearsal/Practice cards, **Crafty Grapple** reaches a cooldown of 10 seconds.

•These Trinkets can additionally be used separately if you want to solely maximize either her Stamina or her cooldown;

• Waxwell can also mitigate the cooldown to 5 seconds temporarily with his Buff, lengthened with Cherished Blanket.

Squirm is considerably one of the best non-Main Character and non-Event extractors in the game, having 5 Extraction Speed alongside an average 3 Star in Skill Check.

With his Active Ability, **Distressed Delicacy**, Squirm can be considered the best extractor in the game. His Ability significantly increases the speed he completes a Machine (doubling his Extraction Speed), making the usual 25.2 second average of Machine completion time go down to an average of 17.53. For the full 10 second duration of his Ability's boost, 30 units of a Machine will be filled. While this makes him the fastest extractor in the game, do note it has a cooldown, hence why a Squirm player should likely stay close to bookshelves around the map, as they make his cooldown deplete twice as fast. This also means he has advantages in certain maps, specifically the Library Floor or Rainbow Rooms. However, maps with less bookshelves, especially the Diner Floors and Sprout's Floor (some of the Diner variants and Sprout's Floor have none), can be less beneficial for Squirm. However, do not waste your time finding and idling next to bookshelves if you don't see the need to do so. By default you’d have to idle by a bookshelf for 40 seconds to fully reduce his cooldown, with one/both cooldown reducing cards you’d have to idle for 37.5/35 seconds respectively. Thus, try to stick by bookshelves for only a fraction of that time, unless all other Machines are currently being extracted. Generally, only idle by bookshelves if you are sure your team has a Machine left for you, and even so, Squirm's normal Extraction Speed is still more than fine. It is possible to eat some bookshelves from the side or back, as well as through certain walls, meaning you are able to hide from Twisteds or distractors while reducing your cooldown. Also, note that if you just use his Ability right as you go on a Machine, by the time Squirm's Extraction boost wears off, you are most likely done with the Machine, so refrain from using it midway unless you are afflicted with Confused or otherwise hindered extraction-wise.

Squirm's main disadvantages are his Stealth and Stamina, both of which can cause trouble when escaping Twisteds or trying to avoid distractors. Though there aren't many ways to mitigate his Stealth, issues with his Stamina can be dulled with the Well-Paced/Endurance Cards, as well as completing Dyle's Floor, and, though not recommended, using Trinkets like Cooler or Speedometer. Though below average, his Statistics are never too big of an issue unless in certain situations, so the best recommendation is to keep notice of where you are going or what dangers are near you in order to be safer. It is also worth noting that winding up his Ability will decrease his Movement Speed by 50% or half (7.5 Walk Speed/12.5 Run Speed), thus it is important to be cautious with when you wind it up, especially if there are ranged Twisteds or fast Twisteds on the Floor; you'd delay your reaction, which can prevent you from breaking line of sight fast enough to avoid damage or using up excess Stamina.

Good Items to focus on are those related to mobility. Stamina Items like Pops and Protein Bars especially can help maintain Squirm's below average Stamina, especially since he relies on it quite a bit with his average speed. Movement Speed boosting Items can help with escaping from Twisteds, reducing the need to use his Stamina somewhat. Extraction related Items like Instructions and Skill Check Candies can make his high extraction even better, especially if they boost Extraction Speed, since that can stack with his Ability. Infact, you can use Instructions as a stand-in for his Ability if it's on cooldown.

Overall, Squirm is a great extractor Toon with little to no downsides, making him a great pick for those who desire to have a great Extraction experience.

**Trinket Combinations**

Some good Trinket sets for Squirm include:

**Mobility**

• **Pink Bow/Options**

•This Trinket enables Squirm to outrun all Twisteds but Twisted Dyle before Panic Mode as well as luring them away from teammates (26.9 run speed). Here are some options to pair Pink Bow with:

• **Speedy Shoes**, to further improve Run Speed (28.2 run speed);

• **Vanity Mirror**, to outrun every Twisted (save for Twisted Dyle) during Panic Mode (35 run speed);

• **Diary**, to not disturb 2 Stealth distractors;

•Only use this Trinket set if there is a distractor that meets such criteria in your team.

• **Train Whistle**, to make escaping with the Slow Debuff easier without losing much Stamina;

•Any of the Trinkets in the **Extraction Section**, to help with Floor progression; etc.

**Extraction**

• **Magnifying Glass/Options**

•This Trinket allows Squirm to take full advantage over his 5 Extraction Speed (1.5 extraction speed) and 3 Star Skill Check (100.5 skill check size). Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:

• **Vee's Remote**, to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote;

• **Participation Award**, to speed up Machine completion by maximizing Skill Check Extraction (19.91 avg/17.7 with Tech Savvy);

• **Stress Ball**, to increase Extraction Speed gradually every successful Skill Check hit, supporting his 5 Star Extraction Speed and stacking with his Ability;

•Any Trinkets listed in the **Mobility** section, to help with survival.

**Ability**

• **Sweet Charm,** to reduce **Distressed Delicacy'**s Ability cooldown (73.6s/36.8s while eating from bookshelves);

• **Ghost Snakes In A Can,** to further reduce **Distressed Delicacy**'s cooldown (68.6s/34.3s while eating from bookshelves).

Waxwell, if used properly, is a really versatile Toon, being a great distractor, decent extractor, and adequate support.

Waxwell's 5 Movement Speed and 2 Star Stealth makes him an almost perfect Distractor, not having the problems other great distractors have, like Pebble's 3 Star Stealth or Looey's need to get hit to be faster. However, he has a major drawback: his Stamina. On top of 1 Star Stamina, his (almost) constant Tired II makes Stamina an extremely limited resource. Although this could be fine with good Stamina management, hard Twisted combinations will be a lot harder, as things like sprint-tapping, maneuvering, or rounding up Twisteds will use up a large chunk of Waxwell's Stamina. Additionally, during Panic Mode, reaching the Elevator will be difficult, especially if really far away, risking death, even with your 5 Star Movement. However, you could have Toons like Astro or Tisha help with mobility, either reducing the need for Stamina or numbing the consequences of using it. You can also use mobility or Stamina Trinkets like Dog Plush or Cooler to ease the weakness. It can be really beneficial to select both Well-Paced/Endurance Cards, as his capacity will be increased to 120. Additionally, his Ability, **Ignite**, can help these Toons use their Abilities more often, letting them help other Toons more efficiently or help you more often. This also removes his Tired II, so you reap more benefits, getting support and more reliable Stamina regeneration. His 2 Star Stealth also lets him solar-kite with Bobette (albeit a Stealth-affecting Trinket is needed), somewhat fixing his Stamina problem and letting him move quick, but certain combos can still be quite dangerous and difficult to handle.

If you want to use Waxwell for extracting, his 5 Star Skill Check still makes him really good with Machines, though his Extraction Speed is quite low. Because of this, he relies on his Skill Checks to let him progress through the Machines, so Trinkets like Magnifying Glass or Participation Award can help him finish faster. He could also use his Ability to reduce the cooldowns of Toons like Shelly or Squirm's Abilities, letting them use their Abilities more and quickening Machine completion. On top of that, his high Movement Speed makes Treadmill Machines also quickly done, albeit the low Stamina makes sprinting on them less common, making it slightly slow. Barnaby Machines are also less of a risk with his high Skill Check, and the coins give a high value, making his low Extraction Speed less of an issue. However, do note the 2 Star Stealth is an issue if you aren't distracting, and certain Machines could be out of reach due to distractors.

Finally, his Ability makes supporting others really easy, with the only downside being his 60 second cooldown and the need to move around. If a player were to stand in the flame trail for the minimum 10 seconds (+5 seconds of lingering), they would have approximately 30 seconds cut from their cooldown, though they could cut even more time if they follow the entire trail, as each flame lasts for 10 seconds (for an overall duration of around 20 seconds, from the first flame spawning, to the last few flames disappearing), meaning a player could theoretically cut down nearly 50 seconds. This maximized cooldown reduction is of course really situational, being reliant on the Waxwell moving for the entirety that his Ability is active, and only really useful on select Toons (e.g. a Toon with a healing Ability, who needs to heal a teammate or multiple, but is held back by their cooldown), as otherwise this could take up time away from extracting from fast extractors.

With his Ability activated, he also glows in Blackouts (albeit really little) and loses the Tired II, letting him move around more quickly and spread his trail. When his Ability is active, you should try running around as much as possible, covering as much area as possible so Toons know where the trail is. You can also put it in a small space and tell Toons where it is so they can simply stay still or move around in the trail. This can especially be done while distracting, though high Stealth Toons will be the only ones able to get to him without endangering the rest. Since he loses his Tired II while his Ability is active, you could use it after being chased to recover Stamina a bit faster, though this should usually only be done if nobody is in need of the cooldown reduction, or won't be affected by it. You could also use it during Panic Mode or a particularly dangerous moment when you absolutely need to recover a bit more Stamina than you otherwise would with the Tired II.

He can be great on Dyle's Floor due to his versatility. His maximum Skill Check means failing is less likely, which can make Twisted Dyle less of a threat, and even if someone fails a Skill Check, Waxwell has the speed to make a quick getaway. He can take care of Treadmill Machines rather efficiently and can use his Ability on certain Toons to get through Machines faster. Plus, the extra +50 Stamina capacity given for completing the Floor can improve his survivability, especially when combined with both Well-Paced/Endurance Cards, since he'll have a capacity of 170, nearly 4 Stars.

In solo runs, his strengths become a lot more apparent. His 5 Star Movement Speed lets him escape almost all of the Twisteds, though without anyone distracting, regenerating and managing Stamina will be harder. His high Skill Check makes doing Machines easier too, also lessening the amount of Skill Check failures and Twisted attractions, albeit the low Extraction Speed makes you stay on them for a while longer. Despite his Ability's main purpose of decreasing others' cooldowns being useless in a solo scenario, the temporary removal of the Tired II Debuff as well as the light produced from the flames can still provide great benefits.

Overall, despite his shortcomings, he is able to adequately do everything so long as you play right. He's really capable of many tasks, but is reliant on good skill and knowledge of the game as well as experience with distracting if you decide to do so with him. He's a very good choice for solo runs due to his high speed and above average extraction, though you'll have to keep an eye on his shortcomings.

**Trinket Combinations**

With Waxwell's 5 Movement Speed and Skill Check and contrastingly subpar Stats, recommended Trinket combinations for him are:

**Mobility**

• **Dog Plush/Options**

•This Trinket will unlock the role of distractor to the holder. (22 Walk Speed) Here are some options to pair Dog Plush with:

• **Speedy Shoes**, to allow Waxwell to outwalk Twisteds slower than Twisted Glisten (enraged) and Twisted Pebble (23.1 Walk Speed);

• **Clown Horn/ Ribbon Spool**, to outwalk even faster Twisteds. Keep in mind this only works half the time, and is best used when duo-distracting (24.2 Walk Speed);

•Do note this Trinket combo is best used when duo-distracting with another player.

• **Vanity Mirror**, to out-run almost all Twisteds during Panic Mode while active, though his low Stamina may reduce this Trinket's use (39 run speed);

• **Train Whistle**, to completely nullify the Slow Debuff, making Twisted Vee significantly easier to distract, and Ichor Leaks much easier to distract in, especially with his low Stamina;

• **Friendship Bracelet**, to be able to sprint for longer periods without a speed debuff, though reliant on multiple alive players;

• **Diary**, to support 2 distractors without taking off Twisteds' aggro;

•Only use this Trinket combination if your distractor has 2 Star Stealth.

• **Scrapbook**, to be able to distract without other 2 Star Stealth Toons taking aggro off you;

•Only use this Trinket combo if most of the players in your run have 2 Star Stealth, or if you're solar distracting with a Bobette lacking Diary.

• **Whispering Flower**, to slightly counteract the Tired II Debuff he has with his Items;

• **Star Pillow**, to regenerate Stamina faster while extracting, taking advantage of his low Stamina and fast extraction, also neutralizing his Debuff;

•The Trinkets below the **Extraction Section**, to help with floor progression; etc.

**Extraction**

• **Magnifying Glass/Options**

•This Trinket allows Waxwell to take full advantage over his 5 Skill Check (167.5 skill check size), especially with his really low Extraction Speed. Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:

• **Vee's Remote**, to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote;

• **Participation Award**, to speed up Machine completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction, supporting his 5 Star Skill Check (24.86 avg/22.59 with Tech Savvy);

•Any Trinkets listed in the **Mobility** section, to help with survival.

**Ability/Support**

• **Ghost Snakes In A Can**, to reduce **Ignite'**s Ability cooldown (55s);

• **Sweet Charm**, to further reduce **Ignite**'s cooldown, though only by a small amount as the Trinket works with percentages (50.2s);

