twisteds.research:
Twisted Connie has two states. Upon spawning on a new Floor, she will have a transparent blue appearance and wander around aimlessly. In this state, she will not attack Toons. You can gather Tapes, Research, and Events' Currencies by going near her without being harmed, similar to Twisted Glisten. She will continue wandering around, occasionally possessing a Machine near her for a short amount of time, producing a blue smoke cloud when transitioning identical to her Toon counterpart's Ability.

If she possesses a completed Machine, it will give an appearance of an almost completed (99%) Machine, but will still contribute towards the completion count. If the Machine is uncompleted, its percentage will stay the same. If she possesses a Machine as a player is extracting, the progress will remain at wherever it was before being possessed. There are four indicators of a Machine being possessed without already knowing beforehand:

•The Machine's valve will be reset to its default position (upside down in the shape of a right-side-up Y);

•The valve of the Machine will rattle;

•The light at the top of the Machine will flash blue and a shaking sound will be heard. This will happen twice before Twisted Connie comes out of the Machine and becomes passive again;

•And you'll receive Tapes when you approach the Machine, if she hasn't been encountered before.

If you interact with a possessed Machine, she will jump out of the Machine to attack you. This attack is unavoidable, and she will go back to her wandering state after. If Twisted Connie possesses a Machine while it is being extracted, the player will automatically stop extracting. Do note that if you do alert her during Machine possession, she will only attack the Toon who extracted the Machine, not any other Toons around it.
